; THE SNAP PAD, and it carries a MEASUREMENT this repo did not have before.
;
; NOT ONE PROPERTY IS SET ON THIS NODE, on purpose. The first cut set radius, rest_height,
; snap_rotation and show_marker = false on it, INLINE (the script assigned directly, not a nested
; PackedScene instance -- the one shape CLOCK-1's trap was documented against). EVERY ONE OF THEM
; WAS DROPPED. The room went 87 packed / 88 live because show_marker never arrived and
; InteractionSlot built its own ring in _Ready. So this build drops an exported C# property set
; in a .tscn in BOTH shapes, not only on a nested instance, and the rule is simply: an [Export]
; is not a level-authoring surface in this project. That is a fourth entry in the ledger
; alongside PropManager.AuthoredKindOf, Carryable.LoadLiftM and RoundClock.Room.
;
; What this pad is therefore made of: InteractionSlot's C# DEFAULTS (radius 0.32 m, vertical
; reach 1.1 m, snap_rotation true, rest_height 0) and a child named SlotMarker that the LEVEL
; authors. InteractionSlot._Ready now adopts a child of that name instead of building one, which
; is a native node name rather than an exported property and therefore cannot be dropped. The
; ring below is drawn at the class's own 0.32 m default radius so the thing a player sees is the
; thing the server measures.
;
; The pad only snaps because the SERVER knows about it. InteractionSlot is a client-side lab type
; (CARRY-1's handoff), so Gameplay registers a PracticePadValidator over every slot it finds in
; the world; that validator answers Snap(pad.RestPose(...)) inside the catch volume and passes
; everything else straight through, so free placement everywhere else in the game is untouched.

[node name="Pad" type="Node3D" parent="PracticeCorner"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -4.55, 0.7, 1.15)
script = ExtResource("12_slot")

[node name="SlotMarker" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="PracticeCorner/Pad"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.012, 0)
mesh = SubResource("TorusMesh_pad")
material_override = SubResource("Mat_pad")

[node name="Table" type="StaticBody3D" parent="PracticeCorner"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -4.55, 0, 0)

[node name="Collision" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="PracticeCorner/Table"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.35, 0)
